# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Felipe Hawthorne et al. (2025). Efficient and Accurate Machine Learning Interatomic Potential for Graphene: Capturing Stress–Strain and Vibrational Properties.
#   The Journal of Physical Chemistry C. doi:10.1021/acs.jpcc.5c03470  arXiv:2505.12140v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.12140v1 (sha256 144614bba1f5331e...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 349 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/hawthorne2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the GPAW LDA AIMD data set of 4- to 32-atom graphene
# cells (NVE, NVT and strained NPT runs, 1.12 million frames plus
# random displacements; 20 % validation), the DeePMD model (se_e2_a
# descriptor, cutoff 8 A, embedding 50/100/200, fitting 3 x 240), and the
# validation RMSEs per system size of Table 1. Elastic constants, phonons,
# VDOS and fracture behaviour are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
